{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr5b375dvnh","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM warm start program note recall blocked by daemon source cluster rewrite","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: the daemon does not merely clip note bodies (write 2000, full_content read 1200). The deeper blocker for recalling a stored world model program is lib/note-source-cluster.js shouldClusterNote: ANY note body >= 1000 chars that looks like source (backticks, def, if (, semicolons) is REWRITTEN on write to a stub (\"Long raw evidence preserved as structured source chunks\") and its raw text is moved into knowledge:source_* evidence nodes. So a code-bearing program note over ~1000 chars is unretrievable whole via /search full_content. Two consequences observed run 13: (1) chunk each program body under 1000 chars to dodge the clusterer; (2) chunk titles must NOT be supersets of the ORIENT query \"game <id> world model program\" or the chunks outrank and crowd out the index note (use \"game <id> program chunk n of N\"). Also: freshly written notes are unreliably searchable under daemon indexing/drain lag, and /overlay/note intermittently 404s under drain load. The chunked-note reassembly path is committed as a FALLBACK behind AgentConfig.chunked_program_notes (default OFF). Live run 13 + live re-seed deferred: the correct fix is a native daemon reassembling note-read endpoint (GET note full body), after which ORIENT reads the single program note directly and the chunk writer/reassembler + flag retire.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T19:08:09.073Z","vec":[-0.07134091854095459,-0.012772650457918644,-0.025868413969874382,0.060710977762937546,0.08331954479217529,-0.025154251605272293,-0.08025802671909332,0.012938684783875942,-0.018440935760736465,0.06691253185272217,0.014327744953334332,0.005566755309700966,-0.02008039876818657,-0.07440897077322006,0.03405185416340828,-0.0015709525905549526,0.03226882591843605,-0.06818702071905136,-0.036